Job Description: HRBP Intern
Greetings from Resolence !!!!

Resolence is looking for motivated and enthusiastic HR graduates who are interested in Human Resources, employee engagement, HR operations, and business partnering. This internship provides an opportunity to gain practical HR experience and develop professional skills in a corporate environment.
Job Details
- Company: Resolence
- Position: HRBP Intern (Human Resources Business Partner Intern)
- Location: RMZ Futura, Block B, Plot No. 14 & 15, Phase 2, HITEC City, Hyderabad – 500081, Telangana
- Work Mode: Work From Office (WFO)
- Working Days: 6 Days a Week
- Working Hours: 9:30 AM – 6:30 PM
- Internship Duration: 6 Months
- Full-Time Opportunity:  ₹3-4 LPA CTC, based on performance and business requirements.
Eligibility Criteria
- MBA/PGDM graduates specializing in Human Resources (HR).
- Eligible batches: 2024, 2025, and 2026, 2027.
- Freshers are welcome to apply.
- Good communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills.
- Interest in HR operations, employee engagement, and people management.
Roles and Responsibilities
- Assist in HR operations and day-to-day HR activities.
- Support employee onboarding, documentation, and induction processes.
- Coordinate employee engagement activities and internal communication.
- Maintain employee records and update HR trackers.
- Assist with attendance, leave records, and HR documentation.
- Support performance management and employee feedback activities.
- Coordinate with employees and internal teams to address HR-related queries.
- Assist in implementing HR policies and maintaining HR process documentation.
Required Skills
- Basic understanding of HR functions and HR practices.
- Good verbal and written communication skills.
- Proficiency in MS Excel, Word, and PowerPoint.
- Strong interpersonal, coordination, and problem-solving skills.
- Attention to detail and the ability to maintain confidentiality.
- Willingness to learn and upskill in HR operations and business partnering.
Internship and Career Opportunity
- Three-month internship with practical corporate HR exposure.
- Opportunity to understand HR operations and employee engagement.
- Develop communication, coordination, and people management skills.
- Potential full-time employment with a CTC of  ₹3-4 LPA, based on internship performance and business requirements.
